# SHA-256 of credentials known to be exposed, so this repository can refuse to
# become another place they live.
#
#   <64-char sha256>  <what it is, and where it leaked>
#
# HASHES ONLY. The plaintext is not here and must never be — a file listing
# secrets in order to protect them is the joke that writes itself.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS, WITH THE SPECIFIC FAILURE THAT CAUSED IT
#
# Across this project I have repeatedly said I would not copy the relay's
# X-FIELD-Relay value into laboratory, and declined to put it in laboratory's
# Actions secrets. Both statements were true when made.
#
# The value was already committed. `41f0b33` (2026-08-16), whose subject is
# "Correct Phase 4: laboratory generates nothing", wrote it out in full inside
# docs/JLAYER-PLAN.md — in the sentence explaining that it is write-capable and
# that laboratory must not hold it. A refusal is a promise, and a promise does
# not scan files.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DO
#
#   DOES. Fails the build if any token in any tracked file hashes to one of
#   these. That covers a paste into source, a doc, a workflow, or an outbox
#   entry, and it needs no plaintext to do it.
#
#   DOES NOT. Remove anything from git history. The relay value remains readable
#   at 41f0b33 and no edit here changes that. Rotation is the only thing that
#   ends it, and rotation is not laboratory's to perform.
#
#   DOES NOT. Detect a secret that is not listed. This is a tripwire for known
#   exposures, not a general scanner — a general one would need to guess what is
#   secret, and would either miss things or cry wolf.
#
# TO ADD ONE: hash it locally and paste the hash. Never the value.
#   printf '%s' 'the-secret' | sha256sum

c3118a4a99dfe805e724cc1da7bba35635e0c09341bf1a25ca9a6fb01e614638  relay shared auth header value (gates POST /d1/execute — write path to production briefs)
5f4af93c436af0f8bd2cce48321f2db14a7b6f6ea3357a25b7073cc426d22e86  BSD API token seen in a screenshot 2026-08
44acccf4a551b57fac8a0aed1fb56bbfac849abefeae735afb199f1704dec48e  Odds API key committed in jubilant-bassoon/docs/source-registry.json
